{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940269-who-are-your-favorite-villains-for-werewolf-the-apocalypse","id":940269,"title":"Who are your favorite \"villains\" for Werewolf: the Apocalypse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T14:52:04-07:00","id":940269,"title":"Who are your favorite \"villains\" for Werewolf: the Apocalypse?","content":"Like the title says, I want to hear who your favorite enemy is in WtA. Either from a ST perspective, player perspective, or both! Who are your favorite sources of conflict for your Garou/Kinfolk/Fera and why? (Don't limit yourself to the game line here if you don't limit it at your table. Maybe it's the Technocracy? Maybe it's Hunters or Wraith?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:02:22-07:00","id":940279,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say who my favorite villain is for WtA. Check out my post in VtM forum under Chicago by Night. It it's bout my Chicago game that had 3 Garou in it. I have had a lot of fun as a ST using Street Fighters as villains. But I try not to limit my self on what I use as a ST. Should have seen the group when a skinny short guy stopped a Suburban by just planting his feet and leaning into his shoulder. Priceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:59:15-07:00","id":940313,"title":"","content":"Fomori are my favorite because it is really easy to create a properly dramatic unique fomori. I have a group of psychic fomori I have used for decades now, that I use as opponents in Werewolf, Vampire, Mage, etc. They are occasionally allies, as well as opponents, so my players never quite know what to make of them, especially when the group sends their Kinfolk birthday cards and, on one memorable session, rescued a group of players when they botched a raid on a Pentex facility. The fact that the group immediately back stabbed them by leading them into the fomori barracks (so the group could make off with Pentex research during the chaos) only produced even more conflicted feelings. Good times...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T23:19:31-07:00","id":940504,"title":"","content":"Pentex. I love Pentex. They can be cartoonishly evil in a way that I find makes for enjoyable opponents. The players can hack into them without feeling too guilty, and as a Storyteller you can go as over the top as you want - &quot;Oh no! You have discovered Pentex's plan burn down the local orphanage in order to transfer the kids to the new Perfect Children Orphanage subsidiary that they run. It's also part of a huge insurance fraud scheme, plus they're just dicks like that.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can also make Pentex pretty dark and use it to tell more personal and disturbing stories. <br /> <br /> Other than Pentex, I tend to use Wraiths quite a bit in my games, sometimes as villains sometimes as allies. Humans are a part of the natural world too, and the actions of werewolves and the people the werewolves fight can often lead to corpses and ghosts. I find that ghosts are a good way to remind players that just because you can turn into a giant wolfman and rip someone in half, that can sometimes cause problems down the road. Ghosts are also a good way to reinforce the idea of Werewolves as &quot;heroes&quot; who mesh out justice for the lives that the Wyrm has taken. <br /> <br /> Basically, wraiths are a good way to let players atone for crimes they've committed or to reinforce the horror that they did. They're also a nice way for players to see immediate results for their actions, as they help a wraith go into transcendence by putting a stop to the monster that killed him in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T00:42:42-07:00","id":941086,"title":"","content":"I'll go with fomori, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T04:45:04-07:00","id":941134,"title":"","content":"SAD, they lack Pentexes cartoonish evil but have an insufferable aarogance that makes me yearn to put them in their place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:17:31-07:00","id":941150,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of the evils that can't be solved by just popping claws, going crinos and preforming a rite of cleansing afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:34:48-07:00","id":941155,"title":"","content":"So the Eldritch Horrors of the Wyrm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T09:22:18-07:00","id":941223,"title":"","content":"Spirals, then Fomori and Garou politics are my favorites.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:04:41-07:00","id":941238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940269-who-are-your-favorite-villains-for-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=941155#post941155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Eldritch Horrors of the Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like the rural town with the closed steel mill, where economic depression, rising crime and drug rates bring about a lot of wyrm problems but it's all just symptoms of the greater problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:40:32-07:00","id":941258,"title":"","content":"Not exactly villains, but I really like using the Red Talons as foils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:07:34-07:00","id":941664,"title":"","content":"I also like the Technocracy as villains. Because Garou are trying to stop the Wyrm corrupting and destroying the world. While the Technocracy is trying to &quot;save the world from the deviants who are warping the world.&quot; It kind of gives the Garou a sort if X Men quality to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T22:42:23-07:00","id":941703,"title":"","content":"I personally love black spirals (small shock i know), but they have such a range to them that I can play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T22:45:14-07:00","id":941706,"title":"","content":"Fera act as interesting foils to Garou. I love running Gurahl NPCs in Garou games, as they are relatively calm and peaceful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T00:19:01-07:00","id":941742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940269-who-are-your-favorite-villains-for-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=941134#post941134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SAD...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't put the SAD as my favorite villain, <i>per se</i>. However, I <i>do</i> sometimes use them as antagonists.<br /> <br /> I had a group of players who were assigned to cover up a little something that an NPC werewolf had done that was turning into a small Veil-breach. It didn't <i>quite</i> go the way I had expected, however. When all was said and done, over a <i>dozen</i> NYPD cops had been dismembered by the pack (the dismembering of four of which had been caught on the video of a police helicopter that was overhead). So the next session, we all sit down to see what interesting things resulted from the little rampage they had had (remember, you can't spell &quot;slaughter&quot; without &quot;laughter&quot;), and without warning, I tell them to turn in their Werewolf characters and I hand them their Project Twilight character sheets instead (which had not been touched in like four years -- presumably mostly forgotten by them at that point).<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, so you get a phone call from that asshole supervisor you hate so much at, like <i>two in the morning</i>. So, guess what he tells you just happened in midtown Manhattan...&quot;<br /> <br /> Classic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}